   145	**Lemma S_p″ (proved; elementary).** Let p be prime, G a set of primes < p with |G| ≥ 4k³, and S the set of products of
   146	exactly k distinct primes of G lying in [Y/2, Y], with 2Y² < p and |S| ≥ C(|G|, k)/(2k). Let T be uniform on F_p^*, and
   147	E(T) the event that the Gauss-reduced primitive vector of Λ_T := {(u, v) ∈ Z² : u ≡ Tv (mod p)} is ±(u, v) with
   148	u, v ∈ S and gcd(u, v) = 1. Then
   149	  #{T : E(T)} = P′ := #{(u, v) ∈ S² : gcd(u, v) = 1} ≥ |S|²/2,  so  Pr[E] ≥ |S|²/(2(p − 1)).
   150	*Proof.*
   151	- **Shared primes** ([rec] Lemma S″ step 2, verbatim): for u ∈ S, the number of v ∈ S sharing a prime with u is
   152	  ≤ k·C(|G| − 1, k − 1) = (k²/|G|)C(|G|, k) ≤ (2k³/|G|)|S|. So P′ ≥ |S|²(1 − 2k³/|G|) ≥ |S|²/2.
   153	- **Injectivity.** Map a coprime pair to T := uv^{−1} mod p (v < p is a unit). If (u, v), (u′, v′) give the same T, then
   154	  uv′ ≡ u′v and |uv′ − u′v| < Y² < p, so uv′ = u′v; coprimality and positivity give (u, v) = (u′, v′).
   155	- **Primitive vector** ([rec] step 5): for such T, the shortest vector s of Λ_T has |det(s, (u, v))| ≤ ‖s‖‖(u, v)‖ ≤ 2Y²
   156	  < p, and every determinant of two lattice vectors is ≡ 0 (mod p), so (u, v) = m·s with m = ±1 by primitivity. So E(T)
   157	  holds for the T of every coprime pair. Conversely E(T) produces a coprime pair with T = uv^{−1}. Hence #{T : E} = P′.
   158	- Divide by |F_p^*| = p − 1. ∎
