   328	So the linear-algebra term ("the 3a term takes over" at L[1/2] for θ > 1/2, [DL] §5) never binds at L[2/5], for any
   329	tuple (Lemma C25(i)): the recursion already makes c_U ≥ 4.129a. At L[1/2] there is no recursion factor 1/(1 − 2^{−1/2})
   330	in the fixed-shape-test constant, which is why 3a could bind there. As in [U], the table entries are grid values and C_γ
   331	is not computed.
