   284	## 6. Theorem DL25 and the cost (proved from U)
   285	
   286	**Theorem DL25.** Fix rationals a, κ, d₀, a′, κ′, d₀′ > 0. DLOG25[τ; τ′] is Las Vegas, and for every prime p and
   287	primitive root g it returns log_g h mod (p − 1) in expected time L_p[2/5, c_DL(τ; τ′) + o(1)], with
   288	  c_DL(τ; τ′) = max( 3a,  a + s + max(a, σ),  a + s + 2^{−2/5}c_U(τ′) ),  s = 2κ(1 + C_γ(τ)),  σ = 2θ₀(d₀, κ)/(5a). (6.1)
   289	*Proof.*
   290	- **Correctness.** Every output is verified (g^X = h); by Lemmas XK1–XK5, HX and T_p-U, A* + XB* ≡ λ (mod n) for the
   291	  true X, so a round with gcd(B*, n) = 1 returns X. The alternation with exhaustive search makes the algorithm
   292	  terminate for small p (where structural guards may fail) and costs a factor ≤ 2.
   293	- **Cost.** Lemma Sel-DL with:
   294	  - 1/p_sel ≤ 4γ^{−1}(16 log p/γ)^{2k}·32k² = L^{s+o(1)} (γ ≥ (log p)^{−C_γ}, 2k log log p = 2κΛ(1 + o(1)); [U] (10.1));
   295	  - M_DL = (d + 1)π(B) + 1 + d = L^{a+o(1)};
   296	  - C_trial ≤ 2F_U(√(2p)) + 2k·T_SQ + poly(d, log p), T_SQ = L^{max(a,σ)+o(1)} ([U] §10), so
   297	    C_trial ≤ L^{max(2^{−2/5}c_U(τ′), max(a, σ))+o(1)};
   298	  - T_post = L^{3a+o(1)} (Proposition XK-U); T_S = L^{a+o(1)}; 1 + log₂ n = L^{o(1)}.
   299	  Total: L^{max(a + s + 2^{−2/5}c_U(τ′), a + s + max(a, σ), 3a) + o(1)}. ∎
   300	
   301	**Corollary DL25′ (arbitrary base; proved from U).** For g, h ∈ F_p^* with h ∈ ⟨g⟩, log_g h mod ord(g) in the same
   302	expected time: [DL] Corollary DL′ verbatim (random auxiliary bases t, primitive with probability ≥ 1/(1 + log₂ n),
   303	doubling budgets with Markov, every output verified, inconsistent congruences discarded).
   304	
   305	**Corollary.** For every α > 2/5, DL in F_p^* in expected L_p[α, o(1)]: L_p[2/5, c] = L_p[α, o(1)].
   306	
   307	**Lemma C25 (the DL constant is the factoring constant; proved).** Write T₁(τ) := a + s + max(a, σ) and
   308	c_U(τ) = max(2a, T₁(τ), (a + s)/(1 − 2^{−2/5})).
   309	- (i) c_DL(τ; τ) = c_U(τ) for every τ; in particular the term 3a never binds.
   310	- (ii) For all τ, τ′: c_DL(τ; τ′) ≥ min(c_U(τ), c_U(τ′)).
   311	- (iii) Hence inf_{τ,τ′} c_DL = inf_τ c_U.
   312	*Proof.* (i) ≤: (a + s) ≤ (1 − 2^{−2/5})c_U(τ), so a + s + 2^{−2/5}c_U(τ) ≤ c_U(τ); T₁ ≤ c_U(τ); and
