   202	## 4. Proposition XK: exact dependencies (proved)
   203	
   204	Fix a kept field A (f irreducible, content 1, 0 < |f_d| < p, m a simple root of f mod p) and rows i = 1..M with
   205	labels (a_i, b_i). Notation:
   206	- K = Q(α), f(α) = 0, t := f_d, β := tα.
   207	- 𝔞 := O_K + αO_K, a fractional ideal.
   208	- For an atom P = (a, b) with gcd(a, b) = 1: 𝔍_P := (a − bα)𝔞^{−1}.
   209	
   210	**Lemma XK0 (ideal bookkeeping; standard).**
   211	- (i) 𝔍_P is integral, and N(𝔍_P) = |F(a, b)|.
   212	- (ii) If r ∤ t·disc(f), the prime ideals of O_K dividing 𝔍_P above r are first-degree, (r, s) with s ≡ ab^{−1}
   213	  (mod r), and v_{(r,s)}(𝔍_P) = v_r(F(a, b)).
   214	- (iii) For each of the O(d log p) primes r ≤ B with r | t·disc(f), an r-maximal order, the primes 𝔯 | r and the
   215	  valuations v_𝔯(𝔍_P) are computable in time poly(d, log r, log p).
   216	
   217	*Proof.*
   218	- (i) Integrality: a − bα ∈ 𝔞. For the norm: f is primitive, so Gauss's content lemma for Dedekind domains (over the
   219	  Galois closure, content(f) = (t)·∏_σ(1, σα)) gives N(𝔞) = |t|^{−1}. Then N(𝔍_P) = |N_{K/Q}(a − bα)|·|t| =
