   260	**Lemma XK4 (unit elimination; proved).** Given s := r_U + 1 ≤ d independent x₁, …, x_s ∈ Λ₁ with entries of at
   261	most β_x bits, one finds a nonzero n ∈ Z^s with Σ_j n_j x_j ∈ Λ₂ in time Õ_d(M(β_x + log p) + (β_x + log p)²).
   262	
   263	*Proof.*
   264	- **Log vectors.** Let Log: K^× → R^{r₁+r₂}, Log(z) = (log|σ_i z|)_{real} ∪ (2 log|σ_j z|)_{complex pairs}, and
   265	  v_j := Log(γ_{x_j}) = Σ_P y_P(x_j)·Log(a_P − b_Pα). These are logs of units, so they lie in the unit lattice
   266	  Λ_U = Log(O_K^×), of rank r_U.
   267	- **Gap (Blanksby–Montgomery 1971).** A non-torsion algebraic integer of degree d′ ≤ d has Mahler measure
   268	  > 1 + 1/(52d′ log 6d′). For a unit z of K, log M(z) ≤ d·‖Log z‖_∞. So every nonzero w ∈ Λ_U has
   269	  ‖w‖_∞ ≥ β_d := log(1 + 1/(52d log 6d))/d > 0. By Kronecker, Log z = 0 iff z ∈ μ_K.
   270	- **Relations exist and are small.**
