   275	    ‖n₀‖ ≤ R := max(1, d!·(2^{O(d²)} max_j‖v_j‖/β_d)^{d}).
   276	    If the coordinate matrix has rank ρ_c < r_U, apply the minor argument at rank ρ_c. If all v_j = 0, any e_j is a
   277	    relation and R = 1 bounds it. That is the E1 case (codex dlog_2 #3).
   278	  - ‖v_j‖ ≤ 2^{β_x}·M·2k·max_P‖Log(a_P − b_Pα)‖, and the last factor is O_d(log p) from both sides:
