   286	  - If n ∉ Rel, then ‖Σ n_j b_j‖ ≥ 2^κβ_d − s√d‖n‖.
   287	  - LLL's first vector b has ‖b‖ ≤ 2^{(s−1)/2}(1 + s√d)R =: R′, and its n-part has ‖n‖ ≤ R′.
   288	  - Choose 2^κβ_d > (1 + s√d)R′. Then b's n-part lies in Rel, since otherwise ‖b‖ > R′. And n ≠ 0, since n = 0 would
   289	    make b = 0.
   290	  - So κ = O_d(β_x + log p).
   291	- **Precision.**
