   152	encodes these comparisons and the further margins named in §§4–6 and 11 (22 checks after codex lv5unif_2 #6); it
   153	compares leading terms only, and is a check of the notes' arithmetic, not an independent proof:
   154	(P1) Y ≥ B^C; (P2) N^{η₀/4} ≥ B^C, ≥ S^C, ≥ 2^{Cd}; (P3) u_F := log X_F/log B ≥ (log log N)^4; (P4) d log d ≤ Λ/C;
   155	(P5) d log S = o(θ log N) and η₀ = o(θ); (P6) log Y ≥ ω(N) log 2 + C log log N, since ω(N) ≤ log N/log B;
   156	(P7) log H/(13d log log H) ≥ C log log N; (P8) μ − ν ≥ η₀ and h − 2ν ≥ η₀ and h − μ + (d−2)ν ≥ η₀;
   157	(P9) 2S² < Y, B < V/2, V < ℓ; (P10) H ≥ dV²·N^{η₀/2}, H ≥ 3dϖ·V, M/V ≥ N^{η₀/2}.
   158	*Proof.* (P8) is the definition of h and the size μ ≈ 1/d ≫ ν + η₀. The others are the listed comparisons of
   159	leading terms: for example, (P1) compares log Y ≍ (log N)^{3/5}(log log N)^{2/5} with log B ≍ (log N)^{2/5}(log log N)^{3/5};
   160	(P2) compares η₀ log N = (log N log log N)^{1/2} with Λ; (P4) compares d log d ≍ (log N)^{1/5}(log log N)^{4/5} with Λ;
   161	(P6) compares log Y with log N/log B ≍ (log N)^{3/5}(log log N)^{−3/5}. ∎
   162	
   163	*Where the asymptotics start (auditU #3, its A8).* The N^{η₀}-type margins in (P2), (P10), (R′4) and Lemma W-U beat
   164	L[2/5]-scale quantities only by a factor D^{1/10}: η₀ log N/Λ = D^{1/10}. For example N^{η₀/4} ≥ B^{C} needs
   165	D ≥ (4Ca)^{10}, i.e. D ≳ 3.7·10⁸ for C = 3 and D ≳ 6·10^{13} for C = 10. So N₀(a, κ, d₀) is astronomical. This affects no
   166	statement: **the algorithm never uses N₀** (FACTOR runs SPLIT and trial division in alternation, [pp] Algorithm
   167	`alg:factor`; Remark `rem:noN0`), and Theorem U is an asymptotic statement about the expected time.
