   504	## 8. Split counting and field selection at growing k
   505	
   506	**Theorem K-U [proved].** Let A be a field returned by SAMPLE_FIELD with δ_A ≥ γ/4. Then one call of
   507	DESCEND_ONCE(A) returns a row or makes a factor exit with probability ≥ (δ_A/(4 log N))^{2k}/(32k²).
   508	*Proof.* |𝒟_A| ≥ γπ_J/4 ≥ 4k³2^{ω(N)} by (P6) and Theorem D-U. The products of k distinct primes of 𝒟_A lie in
   509	(Y^k, (2Y)^k] ⊂ (X2^{−2k}, X]. This range is covered by the k windows [Y′/2, Y′] with Y′ = 2^{i+1}Y^k, 0 ≤ i < k
   510	(all with Y′ ≤ (2Y)^k ≤ X), so one of them holds a set 𝒮 of
   511	≥ C(|𝒟_A|, k)/k ≥ C(|𝒟_A|, k)/(2k) of them (auditU #7), with 2Y′² < N. Lemma S″ ([rec] §3.2) gives Pr_R[E] ≥ |𝒮|²/(2φ(N)) for R uniform on
   512	Q_N, with E: the primitive vector of Λ_R is ±(u, v), u, v ∈ 𝒮 coprime. So Pr_r[E] ≥ |𝒮|²/(2N). With
   513	|𝒮| ≥ (|𝒟_A|/k)^k/(2k), |𝒟_A| ≥ δ_AY/(2 log Y), Y^{2k} ≥ N/(4·16^k) and 2k log Y ≤ log N, this is
   514	≥ (δ_A/(4 log N))^{2k}/(32k²). On E the shape test passes (exactly k distinct primes of 𝒟_A ⊂ J on each side) and
   515	every special-q search returns an atom ([pp] Prop `prop:BS`). ∎
   516	
   517	*Remarks.* No 2^{−ω(N)} (Theorem S′'s loss; 2^ω can be L_N[3/5]^{Θ(1/log log N)}, far above L[2/5]) and no
   518	C(2k, k) (S′'s c_k). The shape-test waste ratio of Theorem K(iii) is not used: every attempt is charged a full
   519	shape test and 2k special-q searches ([rec] §3.2, codex recurse_2).
   520	
   521	**Proposition select-U [proved; sharper than [pp] Prop `prop:select`(ii)].** Let p be the probability that one trial
   522	(SAMPLE_FIELD + DESCEND_ONCE) ends in a factor exit or a row, C_trial a uniform bound on the expected cost of a
   523	trial or of one DESCEND_ONCE, and T_post that of POSTPROCESS. Then
   524	(i) p ≥ (γ/4)(γ/(16 log N))^{2k}/(32k²); (ii) E[cost of SPLIT] ≤ (2M_rows + 1)C_trial/p + 2T_post.
   525	*Proof.* (i): [pp] Prop `prop:select`(i) with Theorem K-U and the set 𝒢* = {A ∉ 𝓡 : δ_A ≥ γ/4} of measure ≥ γ/4.
   526	(ii) (rewritten after auditU #8). Write b for the probability that a trial returns a row, so b ≤ p.
   527	- *Selection.* Trials are i.i.d. until the first factor exit or row; their number is geometric with mean 1/p, so by
   528	  Wald selection costs ≤ C_trial/p.
   529	- *Kept field.* The selection ends with a row with probability b/p, and then the kept field A* has the size-biased law
   530	  Pr[A* ∈ dA] = ς_A𝒜(dA)/b, where ς_A is the per-call row probability of DESCEND_ONCE(A). Hence
   531	  E[1/ς_{A*}] = ∫(1/ς_A)(ς_A/b)𝒜(dA) = Pr_𝒜[ς_A > 0]/b ≤ 1/b.
   532	- *Rows and rounds.* Given A* = A, one round collects M_rows rows in M_rows/ς_A expected calls, then runs POSTPROCESS;
   533	  each round succeeds with conditional probability ≥ 1/2 (Theorem DD), so the expected cost is
   534	  ≤ 2(M_rowsC_trial/ς_A + T_post).
   535	- *Total.* E[cost] ≤ C_trial/p + (b/p)·2(M_rowsC_trial·E[1/ς_{A*}] + T_post) ≤ C_trial/p + 2M_rowsC_trial/p + 2(b/p)T_post
   536	  ≤ (2M_rows + 1)C_trial/p + 2T_post.
   537	([pp] divides T_post by p too; at L[1/2] that was harmless, here it would add s to the 2a term.) ∎
