   542	
   543	[pp] §8 (= lv6 Prop LV6, transferred by ldbound §6.1) is stated for fixed d. Its constants, re-checked:
   544	
   545	- **Lemma C, rows, columns:** degree-free. Computing the roots of f mod r for all r ≤ B costs π(B)·poly(d, log B).
   546	- **Lemma H:** log₂|H| ≤ d log₂|D| + d + ½log₂|disc g| + (d−1)log₂(d + log₂|disc g|). With ‖f‖_∞ ≤ 3MH
   547	  (Lemma GB_w and (P2)): log|D| = log|f_d disc f| = O(d(μ + h)log N + d log d) = O(log N), since d(μ + h) = O(dθ) = O(1);
   548	  and disc g = f_d^{(d−1)(d−2)}disc f gives log|disc g| = O(d²(μ + h)log N + d log d) = O(d log N) (codex lv5unif_2 #5).
   549	  So log|H| = O(d log N) and t_χ := ⌈5d(ln|H|_bd + 2 ln log N)⌉ = O(d² log N). Polynomial.
   550	- **Lemma E (≤ 1 exceptional class per field):** valid for every odd d. Stark's Lemma 8 with c(L) = 4(2d)! for
   551	  L_h = K(√h) (non-normal over Q); Landau with conductors ≤ Δ̄^{1/d}.
   552	- **The factorial threshold and its repair [proved].** ν₁ = min(1/(4(2d)! log Δ̄), c_L/(2 log Δ̄)). Lemma X needs the
   553	  exceptional term 2x^{1−ν₁} to be ≤ x/(40 log x), i.e. ν₁ log x ≥ log(80 log x). The old choice
   554	  log x ≈ (log N)² fails as soon as (2d)! ≫ log N. Take
   555	    s := log x := ⌈(2d)!·(log N + log Δ̄ + d)⁴⌉ (codex's choice; ours was 8(2d)!(log Δ̄)² + (log N)²).
   556	  **Citation (pinned, auditU #10).** J. C. Lagarias and A. M. Odlyzko, "Effective versions of the Chebotarev density
   557	  theorem", in *Algebraic Number Fields: L-functions and Galois properties* (Durham 1975), ed. A. Fröhlich, Academic
   558	  Press, London, 1977, pp. 409–464, **Theorem 1.3**: for L/K Galois, n_L > 1 and x ≥ exp(10 n_L(log d_L)²),
   559	  |π_C(x) − (|C|/|G|)Li(x)| ≤ (|C|/|G|)Li(x^{β₀}) + c₁x·exp(−c₂ n_L^{−1/2}(log x)^{1/2}), c₁, c₂ absolute and effective,
   560	  the β₀ term present only for a real zero β₀ ∈ [1 − (4 log d_L)^{−1}, 1) of ζ_L. This label follows lv6, [pp] Fact `fact:LO`
   561	  and codex auditU_1; Serre (Publ. Math. IHÉS 54 (1981), §2, Théorème 2) restates the same estimate. Pierce–Turnage-
   562	  Butterbaugh–Wood (arXiv 1709.09637) call it "Corollary 1.3". Neither we nor the critics read the label in the
   563	  printed volume (our copy of the scan was not text-extractable); the *content* is confirmed by the literature critic
   564	  against two restatements, and only the content is used.
   565	  Then ν₁s ≥ (log N + log Δ̄)³/(4 log Δ̄) ≫ log(80s) = O(d log d + log log N), and LO's conditions
   566	  s ≥ 20d(log Δ̄)² (log x ≥ 10n_L(log d_L)², n_L = 2d) and c₁x·exp(−c₂s^{1/2}/√(2d)) ≤ x/(40 log x) hold. The base-field
   567	  sampler ([pp] "Sampler") needs ζ_K to have no zero in [1 − 1/(4·d!·log|Δ_K|), 1) beyond what s absorbs; the same s
   568	  works. So Lemma X holds verbatim: Pr_𝔭[χ_𝔭(h) = −1] ≥ 1/(5d) for every h ∉ E ∪ {0}.
