   194	**Lemma W (Wald for adaptive sub-calls) [proved; standard].**
   195	- Setting: a randomised procedure makes sub-calls 1, 2, …. The decision to make call i, and its input m_i, are
   196	  measurable with respect to 𝓕_{i−1}, the history before call i. Call i uses fresh coins and costs C_i, with
   197	  E[C_i | 𝓕_{i−1}, m_i] ≤ F̄ almost surely.
   198	- Conclusion: E[Σ_{i≤τ} C_i] ≤ F̄·E[τ].
   199	
   200	*Proof.* E Σ_i C_i 1{τ ≥ i} = Σ_i E[1{τ ≥ i} E[C_i | 𝓕_{i−1}, m_i]] ≤ F̄ Σ_i Pr[τ ≥ i], by monotone convergence. ∎
