   237	   (Gauss's lemma) gives ker Φ = Q·Z[x, y]_{d−3} with Q = (bx − ay)(b′x − a′y), and Q is primitive, so
   238	   R ↦ QR is a bijection from Z[x, y]_{d−3} ≅ Z^{d−2} onto ker Φ. Its monomial images e_m := Q·x^{d−3−m}y^m
   239	   (0 ≤ m ≤ d−3) are therefore a Z-basis of ker Φ. In coordinates, e_m has entry bb′ at index m, −(ab′ + a′b) at
   240	   m + 1 and aa′ at m + 2, and zero elsewhere.
   241	2. **Triangular parametrisation.** A nonempty fibre is {c₀ + Σ_m λ_m e_m : λ ∈ Z^{d−2}} ∩ C_H. For i ≤ d − 3,
   242	   coordinate i of c₀ + Σλ_m e_m equals c₀,i + bb′λ_i + (ab′ + a′b)(−λ_{i−1}) + aa′λ_{i−2} (terms with negative
   243	   index absent). Given λ₀, …, λ_{i−1}, the condition |c_i| ≤ H confines λ_i to a real interval of length
   244	   2H/(bb′), which contains at most ⌊2H/(bb′)⌋ + 1 integers. Induction over i = 0, …, d−3 gives the count.
   245	   (The last two coordinates only remove further points.)
   246	3. **Probability.** ⌊2H/(bb′)⌋ + 1 ≤ (2H + bb′)/(bb′), so
   247	   Pr ≤ (2H + bb′)^{d−2}/((bb′)^{d−2}(2H + 1)^d) = (1 + (bb′ − 1)/(2H + 1))^{d−2}/((bb′)^{d−2}(2H + 1)²),
   248	   and (1 + 1/d)^{d−2} ≤ e. ∎
