   257	  3^{d−2} forms Q·(±1, 0 coefficients) all lie in ker Φ ∩ C_H, so any bound C_d/(H²(bb′)^{d−2}) needs
   258	  C_d ≥ (3/2)^d/9. Lemma Kern-U's hypothesis bb′ ≤ (2H + 1)/d excludes this; in the design H/V² ≥ dN^{η₀/2} (P10).
