Conditional on Theorem U and its stated chain, I found **no surviving FATAL or MAJOR gap in Theorem DL25**. The new reduction appears sound. Several statements and precision estimates need correction; none changes the claimed \(L_p[2/5]\) exponent or the diagonal constant identity.

| Severity | Location and quoted text | Why | Fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| MINOR | [DL25 L232–239](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dlog25_results.md:232): “\(\|n_0\|_\infty\le R\)”, followed by the Euclidean LLL bound using \(R\) | The displayed argument changes norms without accounting for \(\sqrt{s}\). | Use \(R_2=\sqrt{s}R\) in \(R'\). This adds only \(O(\log d)\) precision bits. |
| MINOR | [DL25 L245–248](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dlog25_results.md:245): roots cost “\(\operatorname{poly}(d,\log p,P)\)” | An unspecified polynomial in \(P=L^{a+o(1)}\) does not establish the subsequent \(L^{2a+o(1)}\) bound. | State the near-linear dependence on requested precision supplied by Pan; see item 4 below. |
| MINOR | [DL25 L210–211](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dlog25_results.md:210): “\(v_r(\operatorname{disc}f)=O(\log p)\) bounds the \(r\)-adic precision” | For the cited implementation using \(\beta=t\alpha\), the starting order has discriminant \(t^{(d-1)(d-2)}\operatorname{disc}f\). | Use the actual starting-order discriminant, whose logarithm is \(O(d\log p)\). Still polynomial. |
| MINOR | [DL25 L172–175](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dlog25_results.md:172): “Every computation … is a function of \(\mathcal T_j\)” | Literally false for generating the labels and evaluating \(g^{a_i}h^{b_i}\). Conditioning on survival of the exhaustive-search wrapper could also reveal timing information. | Define the transcript for the untruncated core after target construction. Analyze the wrapper by domination, without conditioning on its survival. |
| MINOR | [DL25 L35–36](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dlog25_results.md:35), [L328–330](/Volumes/git/factoring-connection/notes/dlog25_results.md:328): “3a … never binds … for any tuple” | Correct on the diagonal \(\tau'=\tau\); false for arbitrary independently chosen tuples in the displayed cost model. | Say explicitly “when the same tuple is used at both levels.” |
